<title>PHILIPPINES: ADB to invest in Indian coal-fired power plant.</title>
<headline>ADB to invest in Indian coal-fired power plant.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Thursday it would invest $15 million in Balagarh Power Company Ltd which will build a 500-megawatt coal-fired thermal power plant in India.</p>
<p>Besides the equity investment, the bank said it was also extending a $25 million loan to the company and arranging a commercial co-financing of up to $100 million under the bank's complementary financing scheme.</p>
<p>The $630 million project involves the construction of two 250 megawatt units of a power plant to be built on an island north of Calcutta.</p>
<p>The project is to start operation by middle of year 2000 which will help cut down a projected power shortfall of 745 megawatt for West Bengal, the bank said.</p>
